---
/**
 * First Year Performance — generated by the `track-record` skill from the 2026-09-24 audit run.
 * Point-in-time by design: regenerate with `node render-astro.mjs` after a new audit
 * rather than editing the figures here by hand.
 *
 * Copy follows profile/voice-and-compliance.md — educational framing, past-performance
 * disclaimer, no "signals", losers shown alongside winners.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="First Year Performance"
  description="Every position published to the Leaving The Matrix community between 2025-06-18 and 2026-09-24, measured against the S&P 500 over matched windows. Educational only."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pb-24 pt-12">

    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-signal">First Year Performance</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-display-md leading-none">My ideas, measured against the S&amp;P 500.</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-bone-dim">
      Every position published to the community between <strong class="text-bone">2025-06-18</strong> and
      <strong class="text-bone">2026-09-24</strong>, priced from the session after it was posted and compared
      with the S&amp;P 500 over the identical window. Winners and losers both.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl border-l-2 border-ink-500 pl-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-mute">
      This is a <strong class="text-bone-dim">point-in-time report</strong> covering that period only. It is
      produced when a full audit is run, not updated continuously, and the figures will not track the market
      after the date above.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl border-l-2 border-ink-500 pl-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-mute">
      It measures <strong class="text-bone-dim">individual research positions published to the community</strong>,
      not my portfolios. Those are tracked separately, live and time-weighted, on the
      <a href="/membership" class="text-signal underline-offset-2 hover:underline">membership page</a>. The two
      sets of figures measure different objects and are not meant to reconcile.
    </p>

    <!-- headline -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded border border-ink-500 bg-gradient-to-b from-ink-700 to-ink-800 p-7 shadow-signal-soft">
      <div class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.17em] text-signal-dim">
        High-conviction positions · average result
      </div>
      <div class="mt-3 font-display text-display-lg leading-none text-signal">+17.8%</div>
      <p class="mt-2 text-bone-dim">
        against <span class="font-mono tabular-nums text-bone">+14.5%</span> for the S&amp;P 500 over the
        same windows, an edge of <span class="font-mono tabular-nums text-bone">+3.3%</span>
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 gap-px overflow-hidden rounded border border-ink-500 bg-ink-500 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="bg-ink-800 px-4 py-3">
        <div class="font-mono text-[9.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.13em] text-bone-mute">Positions</div>
        <div class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-xl tabular-nums text-bone">250</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-ink-800 px-4 py-3">
        <div class="font-mono text-[9.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.13em] text-bone-mute">Names</div>
        <div class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-xl tabular-nums text-bone">91</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-ink-800 px-4 py-3">
        <div class="font-mono text-[9.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.13em] text-bone-mute">In profit</div>
        <div class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-xl tabular-nums text-signal">60%</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-ink-800 px-4 py-3">
        <div class="font-mono text-[9.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.13em] text-bone-mute">Median</div>
        <div class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-xl tabular-nums text-signal">+3.6%</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-ink-800 px-4 py-3">
        <div class="font-mono text-[9.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.13em] text-bone-mute">Closed</div>
        <div class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-xl tabular-nums text-bone">99</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-ink-800 px-4 py-3">
        <div class="font-mono text-[9.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.13em] text-bone-mute">Still held</div>
        <div class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-xl tabular-nums text-bone">151</div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- framework -->
    <section class="mt-16">
      <h2 class="border-b border-ink-500 pb-3 font-display text-2xl">The framework</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-bone-dim">
        Three things have to line up before a name becomes a position for me. It's the same lens I teach
        in Stage 2 of the members path.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded border border-ink-500 border-l-2 border-l-signal-deep bg-ink-800 p-4">
          <div class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-signal">Quality</div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">A business worth owning: durable margins, real growth, a balance sheet that survives a bad year.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded border border-ink-500 border-l-2 border-l-signal-deep bg-ink-800 p-4">
          <div class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-signal">Discount</div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">Bought below what the fundamentals justify, not after the move has already happened.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded border border-ink-500 border-l-2 border-l-signal-deep bg-ink-800 p-4">
          <div class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-signal">Smart-money flow</div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">Institutional, insider and congressional activity confirming the thesis rather than contradicting it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- evidence -->
    <section class="mt-16">
      <h2 class="border-b border-ink-500 pb-3 font-display text-2xl">What the record shows</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-bone-dim">
        <strong class="text-bone">250 high-conviction positions</strong> spanning
        <strong class="text-bone">91 companies</strong> returned
        <strong class="text-signal">+17.8%</strong> on average, against
        <strong class="text-bone">+14.5%</strong> for the S&amp;P 500 bought on the same dates.
        <strong class="text-bone">60%</strong> are in profit; the median position returned +3.6%.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-bone-dim">
        A useful control sits alongside it. Names flagged with the same conviction but never taken as positions
        returned <strong class="text-bone">+13.8%</strong> against
        <strong class="text-bone">+13.6%</strong>, about the same as the index. Spotting a name wasn't what made the
        difference. Actually committing to it was.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-mute">
        The average is concentrated. Excluding the single best position it is +13.8%; excluding the best
        three, +7.3%. Counting each company once rather than per entry gives +24.5%.
        101 of 250 positions are underwater, the worst at −67.0%.
      </p>
    </section>

